<% content_for :title, "ADHD | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-adhd-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-adhd-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-adhd-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-adhd-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ADHD
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>YOUR BRAIN</span>
        <span>HAS OTHER</span>
        <span>FUCKING PLANS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-adhd-intro">
        DISTRACTED. OVERWHELMED.<br>
        BORED. HYPERFOCUSED.<br>
        SOMEHOW ALL AT ONCE.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-pink">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      01 / ADHD
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        IT'S NOT<br>
        JUST GETTING<br>
        DISTRACTED.
      </h2>

      <p>
        ADHD can affect attention, motivation, organization,
        working memory, impulse control, time management,
        emotional regulation, and the ability to get started
        on something even when you genuinely want to do it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes the problem isn't that you can't pay attention.
        It's that your attention doesn't always go where you fucking
        asked it to go.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- EXECUTIVE DYSFUNCTION -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-yellow">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      02 / EXECUTIVE DYSFUNCTION
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        I KNOW<br>
        WHAT TO DO.<br>
        WHY CAN'T I DO IT?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Knowing what needs to happen and actually getting your brain
        to begin are two completely different things.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-callout">
        <p>
          THE TASK CAN BE EASY.<br>
          STARTING THE TASK CAN STILL FEEL IMPOSSIBLE.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Instead of waiting until you magically feel motivated,
        make the beginning stupidly small.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-tool-list">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Open the document.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Put one thing away.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Work for five minutes.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Do the first step — not the entire project.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- DISTRACTION -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-purple">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      03 / DISTRACTION
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        EVERYTHING<br>
        IS SUDDENLY<br>
        INTERESTING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The phone. A noise. Another tab. A completely unrelated idea.
        Something you forgot yesterday. Something you suddenly need
        to Google immediately.
      </p>

      <p>
        Fighting every distraction inside your head can become another
        distraction. Get some of that shit outside your head instead.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-tool-box">

        <h3>PARK THE DISTRACTION.</h3>

        <p>
          Keep paper, a note app, or a scratch document nearby.
          When something unrelated pops into your head, write it down
          instead of immediately following it.
        </p>

        <p>
          You're not saying no forever.
          You're saying <strong>not right fucking now.</strong>
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- TIME -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-black">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      04 / TIME
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        FIVE MINUTES.<br>
        FIVE HOURS.<br>
        WHO KNOWS?
      </h2>

      <p>
        When time is hard to feel internally, make it visible externally.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-tool-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Use timers instead of relying on your sense of time.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Put appointments and deadlines somewhere you can actually see them.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Set an alarm for when you need to start getting ready — not just when you need to leave.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Give yourself transition time between things.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- HYPERFOCUS -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-pink">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      05 / HYPERFOCUS
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        OH LOOK.<br>
        SIX HOURS<br>
        DISAPPEARED.
      </h2>

      <p>
        ADHD isn't always a shortage of attention.
        Sometimes it's getting locked onto one thing so completely
        that everything else disappears.
      </p>

      <p>
        Hyperfocus can feel fucking fantastic when you're making,
        learning, coding, researching, writing, or working on something
        you love.
      </p>

      <p>
        It becomes a problem when food, sleep, appointments,
        responsibilities, or your body stop existing until you finally
        look at the clock.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-callout">
        <p>
          SET INTERRUPTIONS FOR THE THINGS<br>
          YOUR BRAIN WILL OTHERWISE FORGET EXIST.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- OVERWHELM -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-yellow">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      06 / OVERWHELM
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        TOO MUCH.<br>
        SO I DID<br>
        NOTHING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A giant mental list can turn ten manageable tasks into one enormous,
        shapeless monster.
      </p>

      <p>
        Don't ask:
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-big-question">
        HOW DO I GET<br>
        ALL OF THIS DONE?
      </div>

      <p>
        Ask:
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-big-question">
        WHAT IS THE<br>
        NEXT PHYSICAL<br>
        ACTION?
      </div>

      <p>
        Not "clean the apartment."
        Pick up the clothes. Not "fix my finances."
        Open the bank app. Not "work on the website."
        Open the fucking project.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENVIRONMENT -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-purple">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      07 / ENVIRONMENT
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        STOP EXPECTING<br>
        MEMORY TO DO<br>
        EVERYTHING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Build your environment so it remembers things for you.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-tool-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Put important things where you can see them.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Keep things near where you actually use them.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Use alarms, calendars, notes, baskets, hooks, and reminders.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Reduce the number of steps between you and the thing you need to do.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="adhd-callout">
        <p>
          THE SYSTEM DOESN'T HAVE TO LOOK NORMAL.<br>
          IT HAS TO FUCKING WORK.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- IMPULSIVITY -->
  <section class="adhd-section adhd-section-black">

    <div class="adhd-section-number">
      08 / IMPULSIVITY
    </div>

    <div class="adhd-section-content">

      <h2>
        WANT IT.<br>
        DO IT.<br>
        THINK LATER.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Impulsivity can shrink the distance between wanting something
        and acting on it.
      </p>

      <p>
        The goal isn't to magically stop having impulses.
        It's to put something between the impulse and the action.
      </p>

      <div class="adhd-pause">

        <p class="adhd-pause-label">THE PAUSE</p>

        <p>
          I WANT TO DO THIS.
        </p>

        <span>↓</span>

        <p>
          I DON'T HAVE TO DECIDE YET.
        </p>

        <span>↓</span>

        <p>
          WAIT.
        </p>

        <span>↓</span>

        <p>
          DECIDE AGAIN.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="adhd-ending">

    <p class="adhd-ending-small">
      YOUR BRAIN DOESN'T HAVE TO WORK LIKE EVERYONE ELSE'S.
    </p>

    <h2>
      BUILD A LIFE<br>
      THAT WORKS<br>
      WITH IT.
    </h2>

    <p>
      You don't get extra points for making everything harder
      than it needs to be.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX", toolbox_path, class: "adhd-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>